interviews."},"checkpoint_questions":[{"question_number":1,"type":"application","question":"In your own words, what problem does object-oriented design solve?","answer":"Object-oriented design assigns cohesive responsibilities to objects while protecting invariants through encapsulation and clear collaboration.","explanation":"A strong answer states the business or user problem before naming a tool.","skill_tested":"Object-Oriented Design: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":2,"type":"reasoning","question":"How would you apply this capability in the following workplace situation: Model a course enrolment domain where a learner cannot enrol twice and capacity cannot become negative.","answer":"Identify domain responsibilities, model state and behaviour, prefer composition, define contracts and test invariants.","explanation":"The response should describe a controlled, verifiable workflow rather than only a feature.","skill_tested":"Object-Oriented Design: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":3,"type":"application","question":"Compare abstraction, encapsulation, inheritance and polymorphism using one domain example.","answer":"Use Object-oriented design assigns cohesive responsibilities to objects while protecting invariants through encapsulation and clear collaboration. Then describe the workflow: Identify domain responsibilities, model state and behaviour, prefer composition, define contracts and test invariants.","explanation":"Interview answers should connect principle, action, validation and outcome.","skill_tested":"Object-Oriented Design: Workplace Lab & Module Check","difficulty":"Foundation"},{"question_number":4,"type":"application","question":"Identify the main risk in this incorrect approach: Creating inheritance hierarchies for reuse alone or exposing mutable fields publicly.","answer":"The approach is unreliable because it breaks the controls implied by Object-oriented design 