rain and keys, normalise repeated facts, write parameterised queries, control transactions and verify affected rows.","given_information":["SQL","JDBC","Data Modelling"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the apply requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"Persist students, courses and enrolments while preventing duplicate enrolment and preserving referential integrity."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Concatenating SQL strings, omitting constraints or assuming an ORM removes the need to understand queries."}],"final_answer":"Declare table grain and keys, normalise repeated facts, write parameterised queries, control transactions and verify affected rows.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Concatenating SQL strings, omitting constraints or assuming an ORM removes the need to understand queries."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Concatenating SQL strings, omitting constraints or assuming an ORM removes the need to understand queries."}],"memory_support":{"memory_aid":"Avoid this common mistake: Concatenating SQL strings, omitting constraints or assuming an ORM removes the need to understand queries.","mental_model":"Concept → Practice → Proof","quick_recall_note":"Understand → Apply → Validate"},"placement_support":{"question_identification_signals":["Apply","Re